.env
# `.env` alone only matches that exact name. A deployment secret is just as
# likely to land in `.env.production`, `prod.env`, or a `secrets/` directory,
# and the repository is public, so ignore the whole shape rather than one name.
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
secrets/
# Nothing reads a key file today. This becomes load-bearing the moment GitHub
# App JWT authentication lands and a private key is mounted on the host.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
uv.lock
.context/
docker-compose.override.yml
